[{"ref_id":0,"title":"Expected threat (xT): How Match Desk uses it","terms":"Expected threat (xT)","content":"Every pass and carry is scored by the threat it adds. A pass that takes the ball from midfield into the space behind a defence adds a lot; a safe pass sideways adds almost nothing. That is how the desk decides which plays were decisive, and it powers the momentum line: each team's share of threat created over the last few minutes."},{"ref_id":1,"title":"Brackenford FC (BRK): Overview","terms":"Brackenford FC (BRK)","content":"A fictional club in the Meridian League. Formation: 4-3-3. Style: low block and counter."},{"ref_id":2,"title":"Field tilt: Why it matters","terms":"Field tilt","content":"Possession counts every pass, including safe ones in a team's own half. Field tilt only counts the passes that put the opponent under pressure, so it tells you which side is pinning the other back. A team can have less of the ball and still dominate territory, which is common for direct and pressing teams."},{"ref_id":3,"title":"Copperfield FC (CPF): Overview","terms":"Copperfield FC (CPF)","content":"A fictional club in the Meridian League. Formation: 4-4-2. Style: low block and counter."}]
